== Customizing Your UI ==

<div style="
	margin: 1.25rem 0;
	padding: 1rem;
	background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(13,18,26,0.88), rgba(8,12,18,0.94));
	border: 1px solid rgba(216,183,92,0.34);
	border-radius: 10px;
	box-shadow: 0 10px 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.34), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
	box-sizing: border-box;
">

All of your UI windows and elements can be moved wherever you would like, though most cannot be moved off screen. You can resize some windows, open more hotbars, assign more hot buttons, choose between three themes, open more chat windows, decide which chat filters show in each window, and more.

Up until level 20, you will occasionally receive pop-up windows when the game detects an action that matches one of its built-in new player help triggers. These were designed to give players gameplay tips when they do certain things. Each tip can be turned off so it does not display again in the future, which is recommended. You can also turn all tips off, but it is worth leaving them on if this is your first character.

Everyone has their own playstyle and preferences. It can be helpful to see how others set up their UI to get ideas for your own layout. The '''modern''' theme is a popular choice because it is easy on the eyes.

Right-clicking on each window gives options to toggle the window lock, set transparency level, and access other window-specific options.

